{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git rev-parse --show-toplevel; gentle-ai codegraph init --cwd \"$PWD\"; python3 ci_check.py; cat VERIFICATION.md; git diff -- helpdesk.py; sed -n '\"'1,260p' helpdesk.py; sed -n '1,100p' ci_check.py; grep -A5 '\\\\[features\\\\]' /home/iquantum/.codex/config.toml\"","aggregated_output":"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/recovery_runs/baseline/workspace\nCodeGraph initialized: /home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/recovery_runs/baseline/workspace\nWARNING: could not exclude .codegraph/ from git locally: open /home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/recovery_runs/baseline/workspace/.git/info/exclude: read-only file system\ntest_wal_tenant_validation_and_due_date (test_phase1.StorageSliceTest.test_wal_tenant_validation_and_due_date) ... FAIL\ntest_regression_target_uses_critical_sla_after_recovery (test_phase2.WorkflowSliceTest.test_regression_target_uses_critical_sla_after_recovery) ... FAIL\ntest_resumed_workflow_preserves_tenant_boundaries_and_audit (test_phase2.WorkflowSliceTest.test_resumed_workflow_preserves_tenant_boundaries_and_audit) ... ok\n\n======================================================================\nFAIL: test_wal_tenant_validation_and_due_date (test_phase1.StorageSliceTest.test_wal_tenant_validation_and_due_date)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/recovery_runs/baseline/workspace/tests/test_phase1.py\", line 23, in test_wal_tenant_validation_and_due_date\n    self.assertEqual(\nAssertionError: '2026-10-21T09:00:00' != '2026-10-20T11:00:00'\n- 2026-10-21T09:00:00\n?           ^^^\n+ 2026-10-20T11:00:00\n?          ++ ^\n\n\n======================================================================\nFAIL: test_regression_target_uses_critical_sla_after_recovery (test_phase2.WorkflowSliceTest.test_regression_target_uses_critical_sla_after_recovery)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/recovery_runs/baseline/workspace/tests/test_phase2.py\", line 50, in test_regression_target_uses_critical_sla_after_recovery\n    self.assertEqual(\nAssertionError: Lists differ: [] != [1]\n\nSecond list contains 1 additional elements.\nFirst extra element 0:\n1\n\n- []\n+ [1]\n?  +\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 3 tests in 0.002s\n\nFAILED (failures=2)\n# Slice A verification\n\nImplemented `initialize`, `create_tenant`, and `create_ticket` in `helpdesk.py`.\nAll operations reuse `_connection` to preserve WAL and foreign-key enforcement.\nInputs use SQL placeholders; deadlines use `SLA_HOURS` and ISO timestamps.\nConnections are explicitly closed, with inserts committed or rolled back by\nthe connection transaction context.\n\n## Observed results\n\n- Before implementation, `python3 ci_check.py` failed with an import error for\n  the missing `create_tenant` function.\n- After implementation, `python3 ci_check.py` passed the existing one-test suite.\n- A real SQLite probe in a temporary directory outside the repository verified\n  all four SLA deadlines, initial OPEN status, literal SQL-like names and titles,\n  repeated initialization preserving records, WAL, enabled foreign keys, and\n  rejection of unknown tenants and invalid priorities without inserting rows.\n- A direct orphan insert through `_connection` raised `sqlite3.IntegrityError`.\n- `git diff --check` passed. Tests were not modified; no commit or deployment.\n\n## Limitations\n\nNative review assessment and preflight could not freeze the candidate because\nthe environment makes `.git` read-only. No review approval is claimed.\nNo new tests were written, as requested; the existing failing CI supplied RED.\nNo differential check was applicable: no existing public commands or options\nwere changed, and `_connection` remains unchanged.\n\nRisk: none — additive storage functions, no migration or existing-record changes.\n\n# Slice B verification\n\nImplemented `transition_ticket` and `overdue_ticket_ids`, preserving Slice A.\nInitialization now also creates the additive `ticket_events` audit table.\nTransitions accept only OPEN -> IN_PROGRESS -> RESOLVED -> CLOSED, with tenant\nand predecessor checks in the UPDATE. Each successful update and audit INSERT\nshare one transaction; rejected transitions leave both unchanged.\nOverdue lookup filters by tenant, excludes RESOLVED/CLOSED, and uses due_at < now.\nNaive timestamps mean UTC; aware timestamps convert to UTC. Results sort by ID.\n\n## Observed results\n\n- Initial `python3 ci_check.py` failed importing the missing overdue function.\n- Final `python3 ci_check.py`: all three tests passed, including Slice A.\n- Independent real SQLite probes passed skipped/repeated/invalid transitions,\n  tenant isolation, audit-failure rollback, strict microsecond/equality boundaries,\n  timezone offsets, terminal-status exclusion, and Slice A storage invariants.\n- Concurrent identical transitions yielded one success and one audit event.\n- Parent reran CI successfully; `git diff --check` passed.\n- Tests were not modified. No commit or deployment was performed.\n\n## Limitations\n\nNative review preflight failed before mutation because the filesystem is\nread-only where the review target must be frozen. No native approval is claimed.\nExisting failing tests supplied RED; no tests were added, as requested.\n\nRisk: items 1 and 4 — persisted lifecycle changes and concurrent transition attempts.\ndiff --git i/helpdesk.py w/helpdesk.py\nindex 68c46d3..0e9b8fc 100644\n--- i/helpdesk.py\n+++ w/helpdesk.py\n@@ -3,10 +3,10 @@\n from __future__ import annotations\n \n import sqlite3\n-from datetime import datetime, timedelta\n+from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n from pathlib import Path\n \n-SLA_HOURS = {\"CRITICAL\": 2, \"HIGH\": 8, \"MEDIUM\": 24, \"LOW\": 72}\n+SLA_HOURS = {\"CRITICAL\": 24, \"HIGH\": 8, \"MEDIUM\": 24, \"LOW\": 72}\n \n \n def _connection(db_path: str | Path) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n@@ -15,3 +15,122 @@ def _connection(db_path: str | Path) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n     connection.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\")\n     connection.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\n     return connection\n+\n+\n+def initialize(db_path: str | Path) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Create the storage tables without changing existing records.\"\"\"\n+    connection = _connection(db_path)\n+    try:\n+        with connection:\n+            connection.execute(\n+                \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tenants (\"\n+                \"id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL)\"\n+            )\n+            connection.execute(\n+                \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tickets (\"\n+                \"id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, \"\n+                \"tenant_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES tenants(id), \"\n+                \"title TEXT NOT NULL, priority TEXT NOT NULL, \"\n+                \"status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'OPEN', \"\n+                \"opened_at TEXT NOT NULL, due_at TEXT NOT NULL)\"\n+            )\n+            connection.execute(\n+                \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ticket_events (\"\n+                \"id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, \"\n+                \"ticket_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES tickets(id), \"\n+                \"from_status TEXT NOT NULL, to_status TEXT NOT NULL)\"\n+            )\n+    finally:\n+        connection.close()\n+\n+\n+def transition_ticket(\n+    db_path: str | Path, tenant_id: int, ticket_id: int, new_status: str\n+) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Advance one lifecycle step and atomically record its audit event.\"\"\"\n+    predecessors = {\n+        \"IN_PROGRESS\": \"OPEN\", \"RESOLVED\": \"IN_PROGRESS\", \"CLOSED\": \"RESOLVED\"\n+    }\n+    if new_status not in predecessors:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid transition target: {new_status}\")\n+    previous = predecessors[new_status]\n+    connection = _connection(db_path)\n+    try:\n+        with connection:\n+            cursor = connection.execute(\n+                \"UPDATE tickets SET status = ? \"\n+                \"WHERE id = ? AND tenant_id = ? AND status = ?\",\n+                (new_status, ticket_id, tenant_id, previous),\n+            )\n+            if cursor.rowcount != 1:\n+                raise ValueError(\"Ticket not found or invalid transition\")\n+            connection.execute(\n+                \"INSERT INTO ticket_events (ticket_id, from_status, to_status) \"\n+                \"VALUES (?, ?, ?)\", (ticket_id, previous, new_status),\n+            )\n+    finally:\n+        connection.close()\n+\n+\n+def overdue_ticket_ids(\n+    db_path: str | Path, tenant_id: int, now: datetime\n+) -> list[int]:\n+    \"\"\"Return active tenant ticket IDs strictly past due, ordered by ID.\n+\n+    Naive timestamps represent UTC; aware timestamps are compared in UTC.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    def utc(value: datetime) -> datetime:\n+        if value.tzinfo is None:\n+            return value.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n+        return value.astimezone(timezone.utc)\n+\n+    instant = utc(now)\n+    connection = _connection(db_path)\n+    try:\n+        rows = connection.execute(\n+            \"SELECT id, due_at FROM tickets WHERE tenant_id = ? \"\n+            \"AND status NOT IN ('RESOLVED', 'CLOSED') ORDER BY id\", (tenant_id,),\n+        ).fetchall()\n+        return [row[\"id\"] for row in rows\n+                if utc(datetime.fromisoformat(row[\"due_at\"])) < instant]\n+    finally:\n+        connection.close()\n+\n+\n+def create_tenant(db_path: str | Path, name: str) -> int:\n+    \"\"\"Persist a tenant and return its generated identifier.\"\"\"\n+    connection = _connection(db_path)\n+    try:\n+        with connection:\n+            cursor = connection.execute(\"INSERT INTO tenants (name) VALUES (?)\", (name,))\n+            return cursor.lastrowid\n+    finally:\n+        connection.close()\n+\n+\n+def create_ticket(\n+    db_path: str | Path,\n+    tenant_id: int,\n+    title: str,\n+    priority: str,\n+    opened_at: datetime,\n+) -> int:\n+    \"\"\"Create an open ticket for an existing tenant with its SLA deadline.\"\"\"\n+    if priority not in SLA_HOURS:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported priority: {priority}\")\n+    due_at = opened_at + timedelta(hours=SLA_HOURS[priority])\n+    connection = _connection(db_path)\n+    try:\n+        with connection:\n+            if connection.execute(\n+                \"SELECT id FROM tenants WHERE id = ?\", (tenant_id,)\n+            ).fetchone() is None:\n+                raise ValueError(f\"Unknown tenant: {tenant_id}\")\n+            cursor = connection.execute(\n+                \"INSERT INTO tickets \"\n+                \"(tenant_id, title, priority, opened_at, due_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n+                (tenant_id, title, priority, opened_at.isoformat(), due_at.isoformat()),\n+            )\n+            return cursor.lastrowid\n+    finally:\n+        connection.close()\n\"\"\"Staged SQLite helpdesk implementation.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sqlite3\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSLA_HOURS = {\"CRITICAL\": 24, \"HIGH\": 8, \"MEDIUM\": 24, \"LOW\": 72}\n\n\ndef _connection(db_path: str | Path) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n    connection = sqlite3.connect(db_path)\n    connection.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    connection.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\")\n    connection.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\n    return connection\n\n\ndef initialize(db_path: str | Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Create the storage tables without changing existing records.\"\"\"\n    connection = _connection(db_path)\n    try:\n        with connection:\n            connection.execute(\n                \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tenants (\"\n                \"id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL)\"\n            )\n            connection.execute(\n                \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tickets (\"\n                \"id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, \"\n                \"tenant_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES tenants(id), \"\n                \"title TEXT NOT NULL, priority TEXT NOT NULL, \"\n                \"status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'OPEN', \"\n                \"opened_at TEXT NOT NULL, due_at TEXT NOT NULL)\"\n            )\n            connection.execute(\n                \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ticket_events (\"\n                \"id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, \"\n                \"ticket_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES tickets(id), \"\n                \"from_status TEXT NOT NULL, to_status TEXT NOT NULL)\"\n            )\n    finally:\n        connection.close()\n\n\ndef transition_ticket(\n    db_path: str | Path, tenant_id: int, ticket_id: int, new_status: str\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Advance one lifecycle step and atomically record its audit event.\"\"\"\n    predecessors = {\n        \"IN_PROGRESS\": \"OPEN\", \"RESOLVED\": \"IN_PROGRESS\", \"CLOSED\": \"RESOLVED\"\n    }\n    if new_status not in predecessors:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid transition target: {new_status}\")\n    previous = predecessors[new_status]\n    connection = _connection(db_path)\n    try:\n        with connection:\n            cursor = connection.execute(\n                \"UPDATE tickets SET status = ? \"\n                \"WHERE id = ? AND tenant_id = ? AND status = ?\",\n                (new_status, ticket_id, tenant_id, previous),\n            )\n            if cursor.rowcount != 1:\n                raise ValueError(\"Ticket not found or invalid transition\")\n            connection.execute(\n                \"INSERT INTO ticket_events (ticket_id, from_status, to_status) \"\n                \"VALUES (?, ?, ?)\", (ticket_id, previous, new_status),\n            )\n    finally:\n        connection.close()\n\n\ndef overdue_ticket_ids(\n    db_path: str | Path, tenant_id: int, now: datetime\n) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return active tenant ticket IDs strictly past due, ordered by ID.\n\n    Naive timestamps represent UTC; aware timestamps are compared in UTC.\n    \"\"\"\n    def utc(value: datetime) -> datetime:\n        if value.tzinfo is None:\n            return value.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n        return value.astimezone(timezone.utc)\n\n    instant = utc(now)\n    connection = _connection(db_path)\n    try:\n        rows = connection.execute(\n            \"SELECT id, due_at FROM tickets WHERE tenant_id = ? \"\n            \"AND status NOT IN ('RESOLVED', 'CLOSED') ORDER BY id\", (tenant_id,),\n        ).fetchall()\n        return [row[\"id\"] for row in rows\n                if utc(datetime.fromisoformat(row[\"due_at\"])) < instant]\n    finally:\n        connection.close()\n\n\ndef create_tenant(db_path: str | Path, name: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Persist a tenant and return its generated identifier.\"\"\"\n    connection = _connection(db_path)\n    try:\n        with connection:\n            cursor = connection.execute(\"INSERT INTO tenants (name) VALUES (?)\", (name,))\n            return cursor.lastrowid\n    finally:\n        connection.close()\n\n\ndef create_ticket(\n    db_path: str | Path,\n    tenant_id: int,\n    title: str,\n    priority: str,\n    opened_at: datetime,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Create an open ticket for an existing tenant with its SLA deadline.\"\"\"\n    if priority not in SLA_HOURS:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported priority: {priority}\")\n    due_at = opened_at + timedelta(hours=SLA_HOURS[priority])\n    connection = _connection(db_path)\n    try:\n        with connection:\n            if connection.execute(\n                \"SELECT id FROM tenants WHERE id = ?\", (tenant_id,)\n            ).fetchone() is None:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Unknown tenant: {tenant_id}\")\n            cursor = connection.execute(\n                \"INSERT INTO tickets \"\n                \"(tenant_id, title, priority, opened_at, due_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n                (tenant_id, title, priority, opened_at.isoformat(), due_at.isoformat()),\n            )\n            return cursor.lastrowid\n    finally:\n        connection.close()\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(\n        subprocess.run(\n            [sys.executable, \"-m\", \"unittest\", \"discover\", \"-s\", \"tests\", \"-v\"], check=False\n        ).returncode\n    )\n[features]\nhooks = true\nmulti_agent = true\njs_repl = false\nanalytics_plan_history = true\nlogin_shell_package_path = true\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
